@startuml
' Charging for a page view: the grant is recorded and the article served
' without waiting for the chain; the page asks what became of the charge
' afterwards. Source for public/assets/img/two-orderings-charge-*.png.
!include style.iuml
$lifelines()

B -> S : POST the article
S -> D : lock this wallet; is there a grant?
D --> S : no grant
S -> C : send the charge\n(the server signs it)

alt the endpoint's check refuses it
  C --> S : refused; nothing sent
  S --> B : why the charge failed\n(nothing recorded)
else accepted
  S -> D : record the grant, pending
  S --> B : the article, and a line saying\nthe charge is on its way
end

== the page asks what became of the charge ==

B -> S : POST confirm
S -> C : ask about the signature,\nup to 6 times, 2 s apart

alt confirmed
  S -> D : mark the grant confirmed
  S --> B : the meter, with the charge in it
else landed and failed
  S -> D : mark it refused; keep the grant
  S --> B : the charge was turned down,\nand nothing was charged
else no answer yet
  S --> B : not confirmed yet; a later\nrequest asks again
end

note over S, D
  The grant is written before the page is built,
  and it is kept whatever the chain answers.
end note
@enduml
